{"data": [{"author_id": "2087062239819841536", "created_at": "2026-11-02T09:37:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117189266816024802"], "id": "2117189266816024802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Claude Opus: 80.9% on SWE-bench Verified, 45.9% on SWE-bench Pro. Same model, same benchmark family, a 35-point gap. Before you trust a score, ask which version it came from.", "url": "https://x.com/AiSaasRadar/status/2117189266816024802"}, {"author_id": "2035613655828717568", "created_at": "2026-11-03T04:09:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117469289242395034"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 208, "start": 205, "tag": "AI"}]}, "id": "2117469289242395034", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Myth: a higher SWE-bench Verified score always means a better coding model.\nReality: OpenAI stopped reporting it, citing flawed tests and possible training contamination. Which benchmark do you trust now? #AI\n\n— 🦜Kinako", "url": "https://x.com/kinamocchi_tech/status/2117469289242395034"}, {"author_id": "2076817009833021440", "created_at": "2026-11-02T04:00:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117104445376868401"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 146, "start": 135, "tag": "opensource"}], "urls": [{"description": "SWE-bench: Can Language Models Resolve Real-world Github Issues? - SWE-bench/SWE-bench", "display_url": "github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-…", "end": 133, "expanded_url": "https://github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-bench/", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117104452125523968/NK0hpTp7?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117104452125523968/NK0hpTp7?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 110, "status": 200, "title": "GitHub - SWE-bench/SWE-bench: SWE-bench: Can Language Models Resolve Real-world Github Issues?", "unwound_url": "https://github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-bench/", "url": "https://t.co/Yp7tmZTVOz"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/W8a0bWSGKj", "end": 170, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/gitrepos/status/2117104445376868401/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117104443531427840", "start": 147, "url": "https://t.co/W8a0bWSGKj"}]}, "id": "2117104445376868401", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 72, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SWE-bench  ⭐ 6.1k\n\nA benchmark for evaluating large language models on resolving real-world GitHub issues.\n\n🔗 https://t.co/Yp7tmZTVOz\n\n#opensource https://t.co/W8a0bWSGKj", "url": "https://x.com/gitrepos/status/2117104445376868401"}, {"author_id": "1822640978903080960", "created_at": "2026-11-03T13:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117610246017569152"], "id": "2117610246017569152", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI coding benchmarks can make models look much better at software engineering than they actually are.\n\nOpenAI found that 59.4% of the SWE-bench Verified problems they audited had issues with their tests or problem descriptions. They later estimated roughly 30% of SWE-bench Pro", "url": "https://x.com/pradyum1916/status/2117610246017569152"}, {"author_id": "2063863839364706304", "created_at": "2026-11-03T14:21:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117623215224693233"], "id": "2117623215224693233", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 53, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "revolut moved ~2,000 engineers to self-hosted glm 5.3: 30 cents per million tokens, a tenth of the old anthropic/openai bill. claude code and codex survive as \"the exception\".\n\nbest benchmark of 2026 isn't swe-bench. it's what a bank still pays full price for", "url": "https://x.com/belessai/status/2117623215224693233"}, {"author_id": "1956129725635813377", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:27:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322633045999943"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Build apps or SSH into a persistent Linux VM. ssh exe.dev.", "display_url": "exe.dev", "end": 117, "expanded_url": "https://exe.dev", "images": [{"height": 1024, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117468754703728640/X9sqO7sa?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117468754703728640/X9sqO7sa?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 94, "status": 200, "title": "exe.dev - ssh exe.dev", "unwound_url": "https://exe.dev", "url": "https://t.co/kynoDN2j2T"}, {"description": "We ran 12 open-weight models through all 2,294 SWE-bench tasks, 27,528 attempts in all, and published every score, method and attempt. Here are the top-line results, what our own limits did to them, and why this is the baseline for Brain Kitty and Spec Kitty.", "display_url": "spec-kitty.ai/blog/benchmark…", "end": 143, "expanded_url": "https://spec-kitty.ai/blog/benchmarking-open-weight-models-swe-bench", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117322638280515585/-0Vwbba-?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117322638280515585/-0Vwbba-?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 120, "status": 200, "title": "Benchmarking 12 open-weight models on Mirantis TokenFactory and Exe.dev | Spec Kitty", "unwound_url": "https://spec-kitty.ai/blog/benchmarking-open-weight-models-swe-bench", "url": "https://t.co/tUgeCRm5T3"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/TZgc53HUJQ", "end": 167, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/exedev/status/2117322633045999943/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117322166970544128", "start": 144, "url": "https://t.co/TZgc53HUJQ"}]}, "id": "2117322633045999943", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 1521, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Spec Kitty ran 12 open-weight models through the SWE-bench benchmark (with a little help from https://t.co/kynoDN2j2T): https://t.co/tUgeCRm5T3 https://t.co/TZgc53HUJQ", "url": "https://x.com/exedev/status/2117322633045999943"}, {"author_id": "1970407121763119104", "created_at": "2026-11-01T22:23:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117019602169548865"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/arnesh_11/stat…", "end": 84, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arnesh_11/status/2117014452252070050", "start": 61, "url": "https://t.co/9DVV8kEAvQ"}]}, "id": "2117019602169548865", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 3057, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117014452252070050", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "49.5% on ARC AGI 3 public benchmark. You can just do things. https://t.co/9DVV8kEAvQ", "url": "https://x.com/kanishkpaul/status/2117019602169548865"}, {"author_id": "1809599062188204032", "created_at": "2026-11-02T09:22:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117185445868016122"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/syxKcL4pWU", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/bravish_/status/2117185445868016122/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117091066885394432", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/syxKcL4pWU"}]}, "id": "2117185445868016122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 115, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Should your coding agent check its own work before it says \"done\"? Alibaba and Cornell tested 17 ways to add verification to an agent harness. Their advice: skip the self-check.\n\nHarnesses now bolt checks on everywhere: in the prompt, as mid-task reminders, as a gate before https://t.co/syxKcL4pWU", "url": "https://x.com/bravish_/status/2117185445868016122"}, {"author_id": "200924316", "created_at": "2026-11-03T16:50:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117660737610924151"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/MistralAI/stat…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/MistralAI/status/2117562068220195097", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/bJsCp8gJw3"}]}, "id": "2117660737610924151", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117562068220195097", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Mistral cut its new model's memory 16x and it got worse at agent work.\n\nIf you build agents, the technical report behind ML4 is the useful part here, more than the benchmark table.\n\nML4 is 1T total parameters with 52B active, open weights, and it's aimed at long tasks where every https://t.co/bJsCp8gJw3", "url": "https://x.com/x610ck/status/2117660737610924151"}, {"author_id": "1664269804558229509", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:34:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117369827233054961"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jeIyhyrzYL", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AdamHoltererer/status/2117369827233054961/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117369811319562240", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/jeIyhyrzYL"}]}, "id": "2117369827233054961", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 33, "impression_count": 14544, "like_count": 164, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "ARC-AGI-3 is a weird benchmark. \n\nYou can finish an ARC-AGI-3 level and score 1%.\n\nThe score is squared, so taking 10x the human's actions costs you 99% of the level, not 90%.\n\nBut also, the what the \"humans actions\" is, isn't what you would expect.\n\nIt's not an average across https://t.co/jeIyhyrzYL", "url": "https://x.com/AdamHoltererer/status/2117369827233054961"}, {"author_id": "2096651363379814402", "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:57:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117571979397968265"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/uArjtgWtpa", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/0xrompasso/status/2117571979397968265/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117569485452333056", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/uArjtgWtpa"}, {"display_url": "x.com/0xCodio/status…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/0xCodio/status/2109275834984915150", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/pqUyGTn34H"}]}, "id": "2117571979397968265", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 23, "impression_count": 1650, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2109275834984915150", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Opus 5.5 is first on SWE-bench Pro at 89.9% and second on Terminal-Bench 4.0 at 66.4%.\n\nBoth of those hand it the environment. The script you request over the API does not.\n\nThe stale Blender call it writes back is not a hallucination.\n\nThose benchmarks pin a repo at a commit, https://t.co/uArjtgWtpa https://t.co/pqUyGTn34H", "url": "https://x.com/0xrompasso/status/2117571979397968265"}, {"author_id": "2723902960", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:36:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117264467457085580"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 264, "start": 258, "tag": "Qubic"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/vivancosdavid/…", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/vivancosdavid/status/2117213209857859921", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/CzUwJcSTyB"}]}, "id": "2117264467457085580", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 575, "like_count": 43, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 11}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117213209857859921", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Vivancos &amp; Sanchez's Neraxon achieved a new personal record of 0.41 on the ARC-AGI-3 benchmark with a pure CPU without LLM and GPU, evolving more than 100,000 bio-inspired \"brains\" over nearly 180 cycles, and the results and data will be published soon. $Qubic 🌪️💎💟🍀💣☎️🐜🍻🔥 https://t.co/CzUwJcSTyB", "url": "https://x.com/d_de13/status/2117264467457085580"}, {"author_id": "192201556", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:31:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117369081212948876"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/zXRUiOllKc", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/teortaxesTex/status/2117369081212948876/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117367636396822528", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/zXRUiOllKc"}, {"display_url": "x.com/arcprize/statu…", "end": 324, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arcprize/status/2117360588959461708", "start": 301, "url": "https://t.co/XuK9V35Eps"}]}, "id": "2117369081212948876", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 5223, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117360588959461708", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "V4.1F-1017 achieves a non-negligible score on ARC-AGI-3. On par with GPT-6 Sol (High), without any excuses, both in Provider Adapter harness. \nHaiku 5.5 (Max) does 2.8% btw\nAt (max), 6 Sol jumps to 23%. 6.1 saturates the benchmark, for less. But that's a start.\n15% next time. https://t.co/zXRUiOllKc https://t.co/XuK9V35Eps", "url": "https://x.com/teortaxesTex/status/2117369081212948876"}, {"author_id": "177456343", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:43:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117598582614180328"], "id": "2117598582614180328", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 82, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Mistral's Large 4 technical report has a lesson for anyone building AI agents. Cheaper memory can quietly break the work you actually care about.\n\nMistral first stacked sliding windows and layer-to-layer cache sharing to cut the model's KV cache by 16x. Pretraining evals looked", "url": "https://x.com/Abdur_sayeed/status/2117598582614180328"}, {"author_id": "1374912794", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:37:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117264821372457297"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/KkSVNI2MPq", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/vibelancer/status/2117264821372457297/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117263093302448128", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/KkSVNI2MPq"}, {"display_url": "x.com/rimtoln/status…", "end": 316, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/rimtoln/status/2117217154055462972", "start": 293, "url": "https://t.co/CMuUbpmAGa"}]}, "id": "2117264821372457297", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 2788, "like_count": 65, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 32, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117217154055462972", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "MICROSOFT TOKENECONOMIZER CUTS CLAUDE CODE AND CODEX COSTS UP TO 30.9% WITHOUT TOUCHING THE MODEL\n\nMicrosoft and UC Berkeley open-sourced it. On 277 SWE-Bench tasks, mean cost dropped 18.4-30.9% across 5 agent-model setups.\n\nThe whole trick fits in 1 repo and 3 moves: https://t.co/KkSVNI2MPq https://t.co/CMuUbpmAGa", "url": "https://x.com/vibelancer/status/2117264821372457297"}, {"author_id": "1623470370119380992", "created_at": "2026-11-02T08:40:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117174875701780946"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/LryVS1A7VO", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cryptofanatiix/status/2117174875701780946/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116993711372419072", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/LryVS1A7VO"}]}, "id": "2117174875701780946", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1047, "like_count": 61, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "0.38. That’s Qubic’s best score on ARC-AGI-3 so far, up from 0.13 when the work started, on a brain under 200 neurons with zero GPUs.\n\nIt reportedly sits ahead of some Grok 4.5 and Claude 4.7 results on that same test.\n\nThat’s a threshold, not an oracle. One benchmark, one https://t.co/LryVS1A7VO", "url": "https://x.com/cryptofanatiix/status/2117174875701780946"}, {"author_id": "1099226694085459968", "created_at": "2026-11-03T16:55:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117662078559302116"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/VivancosDavid/…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/VivancosDavid/status/2117577761980027228", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/19OUvQeeNy"}]}, "id": "2117662078559302116", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 364, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 4}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117577761980027228", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "155,192 evolved brains. 100 GB. Open on Hugging Face. No LLMs, no GPUs.\n\nThese Neuraxon brains were bred over 114+ architecture search runs on the public ARC-AGI-3 games, the benchmark built to test whether AI can actually learn new tasks like humans do.\n\nWhile everyone races to https://t.co/19OUvQeeNy", "url": "https://x.com/BaierMiroslav/status/2117662078559302116"}, {"author_id": "1759191266581966848", "created_at": "2026-11-03T19:49:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117705850634858986"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/4uQlsqALXY", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MaryamMiradi/status/2117705850634858986/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117705838504689664", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/4uQlsqALXY"}]}, "id": "2117705850634858986", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 313, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🛠️🧭 I went down the AI Agent evaluation rabbit hole.\n\nIf you are building AI Agents for production, you have to evaluate much more than the final answer:\n\ntool calls, retrieval quality, reasoning paths, failed steps, latency, cost, safety and regressions.\n\nSo I went through the https://t.co/4uQlsqALXY", "url": "https://x.com/MaryamMiradi/status/2117705850634858986"}, {"author_id": "979737336", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117595149769560293"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/83RrXYYJWp", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cutetoxicguy/status/2117595149769560293/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117526603097923584", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/83RrXYYJWp"}]}, "id": "2117595149769560293", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🧠 NVIDIA built a 4B-parameter language model that can become more capable simply by running parts of its own network multiple times.\n\nNo extra weights. No model switching. No additional training required when changing the compute budget.\n\nMeet Nemotron Labs Dory 1.0-4B, an https://t.co/83RrXYYJWp", "url": "https://x.com/cutetoxicguy/status/2117595149769560293"}, {"article": {"title": "Stages of AI: Two Years Later"}, "author_id": "1709302428150169600", "created_at": "2026-11-02T05:09:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117121969674178827"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2117…", "end": 232, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2117120129683316736", "start": 209, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2117120129683316736", "url": "https://t.co/51BsAIzckq"}]}, "id": "2117121969674178827", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 69, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI's five stages of AI, two years on: Level 3 shipped, Level 4 is the fight, Level 5 is a horizon. Rewritten — with the part nobody quotes, which is that the company that drew the ladder stopped using it. https://t.co/51BsAIzckq", "url": "https://x.com/peacenjunity/status/2117121969674178827"}, {"article": {"title": "Agents are still job hoppers"}, "author_id": "2055671535860600832", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:51:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117283352864862716"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2117…", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/